================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
================================================================================

The MIT grant above covers the original work in this repository: the notebooks,
the build tooling, the stylesheet and scripts, the book's prose, and the figures
drawn for it.

Two sets of files are redistributed here under their own terms, and those terms
travel with the files rather than being altered by the licence above. Both are
MIT, so there is no restriction on this repository that the licence above does
not already state. `book/images/CREDITS.md` is the long-form record.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. book/images/transformer-explainer/    — MIT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Five figures from Transformer Explainer by the Polo Club of Data Science at
Georgia Tech:

    https://poloclub.github.io/transformer-explainer/
    https://github.com/poloclub/transformer-explainer

    MIT License. Copyright (c) 2022 Polo Club of Data Science.

The full notice is kept verbatim alongside the files, in
book/images/transformer-explainer/LICENSE.txt, which is what the licence
requires of anyone redistributing them. Do not delete it.

Paper: Cho, A., Kim, G. C., Karpekov, A., Helbling, A., Wang, Z. J., Lee, S.,
Hoover, B., and Chau, D. H. "Transformer Explainer: Learning LLM Transformers
with Interactive Visual Explanation and Experimentation." CHI 2026.
arXiv:2408.04619.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. book/vendor/katex/    — MIT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

KaTeX, which renders the book's mathematics offline so the page needs no
network access:

    https://katex.org  /  https://github.com/KaTeX/KaTeX

    MIT License. Copyright (c) 2013-2020 Khan Academy and other contributors.

The full notice is kept at book/vendor/katex/LICENSE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Linked, not included
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every diagram in the book is drawn for it, in `book/chapters/*.html` as inline
SVG. Two widely-read explanations shaped how those diagrams are laid out and are
credited in the text where their framing is used:

    Christopher Olah, "Understanding LSTMs"
    https://colah.github.io/posts/2015-08-Understanding-LSTMs/
    The "conveyor belt" reading of the cell state is his, credited in chapter 05.

    Jay Alammar, "The Illustrated Transformer"
    https://jalammar.github.io/illustrated-transformer/
    Linked from chapter 06 as further reading.

Neither carries a licence that would permit reproducing its figures here — Olah's
states none at all — so none of their images are in this repository, and none
should be added without written permission from the author.

The NLTK corpora the notebooks use (movie_reviews, gutenberg, comtrans, punkt)
are downloaded at runtime to ~/nltk_data/ and are not redistributed here. Each
carries its own licence, which `nltk.download()` reports.
